{"ts": "2026-09-14T02:23:19.680195+00:00", "run_id": "01a09db9-a037-7cf6-a583-2401f53fcbd8", "type": "token", "seq": 135, "payload": {"text": "-monitoring-supplies"}}
{"ts": "2026-09-14T02:23:19.718283+00:00", "run_id": "01a09db9-a037-7cf6-a583-2401f53fcbd8", "type": "answer", "seq": 136, "payload": {"summary": "For Medicare to cover a Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM), the following practitioner visit requirements must be met: ## Initial Coverage Visit As part of the **initial provision** of a CGM, the treating practitioner must conduct an **in-person or Medicare-approved telehealth visit** with the beneficiary. The medical record from that visit must document that: 1. The beneficiary has **diabetes mellitus** 2. The beneficiary (or caregiver) has received **appropriate training** in the use of the CGM, evidenced by a prescription 3. The CGM is prescribed in accordance with **FDA indications for use** 4. The CGM is prescribed to improve glycemic control for a beneficiary who is **insulin-treated** or has a **history of problematic hypoglycemia** ## Continued Coverage Visit To justify **continued coverage**, the treating practitioner must conduct an **in-person or Medicare-approved telehealth visit with the beneficiary every 6 months** following the initial prescription. The visit must document", "body_markdown": "For Medicare to cover a Continuous Glucose Monitor (CGM), the following practitioner visit requirements must be met:\n\n## Initial Coverage Visit\nAs part of the **initial provision** of a CGM, the treating practitioner must conduct an **in-person or Medicare-approved telehealth visit** with the beneficiary. The medical record from that visit must document that:\n1. The beneficiary has **diabetes mellitus**\n2. The beneficiary (or caregiver) has received **appropriate training** in the use of the CGM, evidenced by a prescription\n3. The CGM is prescribed in accordance with **FDA indications for use**\n4. The CGM is prescribed to improve glycemic control for a beneficiary who is **insulin-treated** or has a **history of problematic hypoglycemia**\n\n## Continued Coverage Visit\nTo justify **continued coverage**, the treating practitioner must conduct an **in-person or Medicare-approved telehealth visit with the beneficiary every 6 months** following the initial prescription. The visit must document:\n- The beneficiary's **adherence to their CGM regimen and diabetes treatment plan**\n- That the supplies remain **medically necessary**\n\n**Note:** There is no requirement for the practitioner to reconfirm that the initial coverage criteria are met for continued coverage—only the 6-month adherence visit is required.\n\nFailure to document this 6-month visit can result in insufficient documentation errors and payment recoupment.\n\nSources:\n- CMS Glucose Monitors LCD (L33822): https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33822\n- CMS Policy Article A52464: https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52464\n- CMS Response to Comments (A59330): https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleId=59330&ver=6\n- CMS Compliance Tips for Glucose Monitoring Supplies: https://www.cms.gov/training-education/medicare-learning-networkr-mln/compliance/medicare-provider-compliance-tips/glucose-monitoring-supplies", "claims": [], "citations": [{"n": 1, "evidence_id": "", "doc_id": "", "url": "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33822", "label": "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33822"}, {"n": 2, "evidence_id": "", "doc_id": "", "url": "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52464", "label": "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52464"}, {"n": 3, "evidence_id": "", "doc_id": "", "url": "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleId=59330&ver=6", "label": "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleId=59330&ver=6"}, {"n": 4, "evidence_id": "", "doc_id": "", "url": "https://www.cms.gov/training-education/medicare-learning-networkr-mln/compliance/medicare-provider-compliance-tips/glucose-monitoring-supplies", "label": "https://www.cms.gov/training-education/medicare-learning-networkr-mln/compliance/medicare-provider-compliance-tips/glucose-monitoring-supplies"}], "effective_dates": [], "contradictions": [], "unknowns": [], "confidence": 0.0, "scope_warning": null}}
